<DIV><FONT size="1" style="font-size:1pt;color:white">273Q25 Financial Results Outlook Net Interest  Income Noninterest  Expense Expect 2025 net interest income (NII) to be roughly in line with 2024 NII of  $47.7&nbsp;billion, unchanged from prior guidance  &#8226; Expect 4Q25 net interest income to be ~$12.4-$12.5 billion &#8226; Net interest income performance will ultimately be determined by a variety of factors,  many of which are uncertain, including the absolute level of rates and the shape of the  yield curve; deposit balances, mix and pricing; and loan demand  Expect 2025 noninterest expense to be ~$54.6 billion, up from prior guidance of  ~$54.2 billion, and includes:  &#8226; Higher severance expense of ~$200 million &#8226; Higher revenue-related compensation expense of ~$200 million, predominantly in WIM,  driven by strong market performance in the second half of 2025 Expect 4Q25 noninterest expense to be ~$13.5 billion </FONT></DIV>
